    "q-89745": {
      "dom_id": "step-q89745",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ 1-\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}, & x\\ge 1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(X\\le 2).$",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a continuous random variable $X$ is the function $F(x)$ defined by\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nHence, the required probability is $F(2)=1-\\frac{1}{{2}^{6}}=\\frac{63}{64}.$",
